mutter on SPARC: keep upstream's GSK_RENDERER=cairo in mutter-x11-frames.

patches/12-37245012.patch (from oracle/solaris-userland, where it is
12-37245012.patch.i386) removes it, reverting
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/commit/57fdd7efd2d2ef05df86c60e36e200a15a9918a0
Oracle applies that only on i386 "since its causing rendering and
performance issues on sparc" with the GL renderer.  This puts the line back
on SPARC, so SPARC builds behave as upstream mutter and as Solaris SPARC,
while x86 keeps the patch set it has.  Applied on SPARC only (Makefile,
ADDITIONAL_PATCHES).

--- a/src/frames/main.c
+++ b/src/frames/main.c
@@ -42,6 +42,8 @@
   GMainLoop *loop;
   Display *xdisplay;
 
+  g_setenv ("GSK_RENDERER", "cairo", TRUE);
+
   /* We do know the desired GDK backend, don't let
    * anyone tell us otherwise.
    */
